    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a5">

                <pb facs="0664" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg616"/>

                <head>Mr. Van Valkenburgh to Sir Harry S. Parkes.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Osaka,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 14, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I desire, through you, to express my thanks
                    to J. Frederick Lowder, esq., her Britannic Majesty’s acting vice-consul at
                    Osaka, for the prompt and energetic measures adopted by him on the occasion of
                    the recent sad accident, by which he was enabled to recover the body of
                    Rear-Admiral H. H. Bell, and also in furnishing to me the first information I
                    received of the misfortune.</p>
                <p>I shall take pleasure in transmitting to my government an account of his humane
                    exertions.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the
                            United States.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi> S. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Parkes,</hi> K. C. B., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;., Osaka.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
